{
  "dom_id": "step-q163061",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{sin}\u2061y,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=6\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.",
  "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=6\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\u222c}_{D}x\\cdot 6\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}6x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y}6x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y\\cdot {[{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3{sin}^{2}\u2061y\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[{sin}^{3}\u2061y]}_{y=0}^{y=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
